{
  "id": "d1-export:en:performance-max-vs-search-2026",
  "slug": "performance-max-vs-search-2026",
  "status": "published",
  "data": {
    "title": "Performance Max vs Search Campaigns: The 2026 Guide",
    "excerpt": "Performance Max vs Search in 2026: how Google decides which one serves, what changed in PMax reporting, and a simple way to run both without overlap.",
    "content": [
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "When Performance Max launched, many PPC managers treated it as a black box that ate their brand traffic. By 2026 the picture is clearer: Google has spelled out how it chooses between the two campaign types and has opened up much of the reporting. The answer isn't \"one or the other\"; it's knowing which job each one does and setting rules so they don't fight over the same searches.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "The short answer",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Use Search",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " to protect your brand terms and the high-intent queries where you need to see and control exactly what triggers each click.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Use Performance Max",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " when you have conversion goals and good assets (or a Merchant Center feed) and want to reach people across YouTube, Display, Search, Discover, Gmail and Maps from one campaign.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Run both",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " when you can afford it, with exact match keywords in Search, negative keywords in Performance Max and a weekly look at the search terms report.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "How Google decides between Search and Performance Max",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/10724817?hl=en"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Performance Max is, in Google's words, \"a goal-based campaign type that allows you to access all Google Ads inventory\" from a single campaign. The overlap with Search is handled by a priority rule that Google documents in its Help Center (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google Ads Help: About Performance Max campaigns",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "):",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Exact match wins.",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " Search campaigns with an exact match keyword are prioritized over Performance Max when the query matches that keyword exactly.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Search themes are not exact match.",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " The search themes you add to Performance Max carry the same priority as phrase and broad match keywords.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "What it means in practice:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " if a query matters to you, put it in a Search campaign as exact match. Everything you leave to phrase match, broad match or search themes is territory both campaign types can compete for.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "What changed: Performance Max is less of a black box",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/16451273?hl=en"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "In a Help Center update from August 7, 2025, Google listed the visibility and control features now available in Performance Max (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google Ads Help: More visibility and control in Performance Max",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "):",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Campaign-level negative keywords",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " for all Performance Max campaigns, applying to Search and Shopping inventory, plus the option to apply negative keyword lists.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Search terms reporting",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " for all Performance Max campaigns, also through the API.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Channel performance report",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ", launched in beta at Google Marketing Live, to see results by surface.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Full asset stats",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " with conversions, cost and clicks, and the option to see and remove assets created with text customization and final URL expansion.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "More search themes:",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " up to 50 per asset group, up from 25.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Device and age targeting",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": " fully available, with gender controls in beta.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ],
        "listItem": "bullet",
        "level": 1
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Many of the old arguments for keeping Performance Max away from your account were about not seeing search terms or not being able to exclude them. Those arguments are now weaker.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "The middle ground: AI Max for Search campaigns",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "https://blog.google/products/ads-commerce/google-ai-max-for-search-campaigns/"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "In May 2025 Google introduced ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "AI Max for Search campaigns",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": ", a one-click suite of targeting and creative features that you turn on inside a Search campaign (",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google, May 6, 2025",
            "marks": [
              "l0"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "). It uses your keywords, assets and landing pages to match more queries and to generate ad text, while you keep the reporting and structure of Search.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Google says advertisers who activate it typically see 14% more conversions or conversion value at a similar CPA or ROAS, and 27% for campaigns still running mostly exact and phrase match keywords. Those figures come from Google's internal data and exclude retail advertisers, so treat them as Google's claim, not a benchmark for your account. For a lead generation business that wants more reach without giving up Search, AI Max is worth testing before jumping to Performance Max.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "When each one fits",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h3",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Performance Max fits when",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [
          {
            "_key": "l0",
            "_type": "link",
            "href": "/en/posts/google-lens-shopping-ads-sales-channel-2026"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "You sell products with a ",
            "marks": []
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Merchant Center feed",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "_type": "span",
