      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "It can overlap. Google prioritizes a Search campaign when the query is identical to one of its exact match keywords; otherwise Performance Max can compete for the same searches. Keep your key terms as exact match in Search and use negative keywords in Performance Max.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h3",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Can I add negative keywords to Performance Max?",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "Yes. In 2025 Google rolled out campaign-level negative keywords to all Performance Max campaigns, applying to Search and Shopping inventory, and added the option to apply negative keyword lists.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "h3",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "What is AI Max for Search campaigns?",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "text": "It's a one-click suite of targeting and creative features that Google launched in beta in May 2025 inside Search campaigns. It expands matching beyond your keywords and generates ad text from your landing pages, while you keep a Search campaign structure.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
